    <string name="service_dialog_title">Turn on the PaperScreen service</string>
    <string name="service_dialog_message">PaperScreen draws its filtered screen as an accessibility overlay. That\'s the only kind of overlay Android lets be fully opaque while your taps still reach the apps underneath. The same service captures each window underneath the overlay, so the overlay never has to get out of the way. Captures stay on your phone.\n\nOn the next screen, open Installed apps (or Downloaded apps), choose PaperScreen, and turn it on. Then come back here.</string>
    <string name="service_dialog_restricted">\n\nIf the switch is greyed out as a \"restricted setting\", open App info for PaperScreen, tap ⋮ in the top corner, choose \"Allow restricted settings\", and try again.</string>
